---

<article class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
      Discount Pricing & Early Payment Incentive Calculator Guide
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Offering strategic discounts—such as early payment terms (2/10 Net 30), bulk purchasing savings, or seasonal promotional rates—can accelerate client payment collection cycles and boost conversion rates on new sales proposals.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Formula Box */}
  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-purple-400">
      Discount & Savings Formulas
    </h3>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-purple-950/40 border border-purple-500/30 text-center font-mono text-sm sm:text-base text-white font-bold">
      Discount Amount = Original Price × (Discount Percentage / 100)<br/>
      Final Discounted Price = Original Price - Discount Amount
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Percentage discounts subtract a proportional ratio from the base selling price. When applying stackable discounts or early payment incentives, calculate each discount sequentially on the net subtotal before adding sales tax.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Worked Numerical Example */}
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Worked Numerical Example: Early Payment Incentive (2/10 Net 30)
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A consulting firm issues a $5,000 invoice with "2/10 Net 30" payment terms (offering a 2% discount if paid within 10 days):
    </p>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400"><span>1. Original Base Invoice Amount:</span><span class="text-slate-200">$5,000.00</span></div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400"><span>2. Early Payment Discount Rate (2%):</span><span class="text-purple-300">2.00%</span></div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400"><span>3. Total Savings Amount ($5,000 × 0.02):</span><span class="text-emerald-400">-$100.00</span></div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-white font-bold border-t border-slate-800 pt-1.5 text-sm"><span>Final Discounted Amount Payable:</span><span class="text-purple-400">$4,900.00</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Practical Freelancer Advice */}
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Best Practices for Discounting Without Devaluing Your Services
    </h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Trade Discounts for Value:</strong> Never offer price cuts for free. Request something in return, such as a 50% upfront deposit, a longer contract commitment, or a client case study testimonial.</li>
      <li><strong>Use Early Payment Terms (2/10 Net 30):</strong> A 2% discount paid in 10 days improves your working capital cash flow far more than waiting 60+ days for corporate checks.</li>
      <li><strong>Display Discounts Clearly on Invoices:</strong> Itemize the original price, the discount savings row, and the final price to highlight value delivered to the client.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {/* Frequently Asked Questions */}
  <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Frequently Asked Questions About Discounts
    </h3>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">What does 2/10 Net 30 mean on an invoice?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">It means the client receives a 2% discount if they pay the invoice within 10 days; otherwise, the full invoice amount is due within 30 days.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Do I apply sales tax before or after the discount?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Sales tax is calculated on the discounted net price, not the original price, because sales tax is levied on the actual gross amount paid by the customer.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">How do stacked discounts work?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">If a client receives a 10% volume discount plus a 5% early payment discount, apply the 10% first to get a reduced subtotal, and then apply the 5% to that reduced subtotal (yielding a total effective discount of 14.5%, not 15%).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Can I calculate percentage savings with this tool?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Yes! Enter the original price and discount percentage to calculate exact savings and final cost instantly.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-1">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Is my commercial data safe?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Yes. SimpleInvoiceTools operates 100% locally in your browser with zero data logging.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
